# Keep the Docker build context lean for Dockerfile.serve and Dockerfile.hostile.
# Everything the Go builds need stays: sources, go.mod/sum, the embedded *.bd
# assets, testdata/ (the hostile image runs the whole Go suite) and build/
# minus build/bin — main.go embeds build/appicon.png, and wails.json plus the
# platform folders are read by tooling, so only the compiled output goes.
# frontend/dist is regenerated as a stub inside Dockerfile.hostile, so excluding
# the (usually symlinked) node_modules and any stale dist is safe.
.git
frontend/node_modules
frontend/dist
build/bin
doc/build

# Local, gitignored trees that can be very large: sibling parser checkouts
# and gnubg sources (they are Go modules fetched by go.mod, never read from
# here), Python virtualenvs, the downloaded two-sided bearoff table and its
# partial downloads, scratch space, task sheets and Claude Code config.
gnubg/
xgparser/
gnubgparser/
bgfparser/
.venv
doc/.venv
gnubg_ts6x11.bd
*.bd.part
tmp/
tasks/
.claude/

# Databases opened at the repo root (and their WAL/lock companions) must
# never end up in an image.
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
*.db.lock
